   "title": "ὃ, not ὅς",
   "claim": "contested (emphasis)",
   "body": "The relative is neuter — “that which” — four times in v.1, not masculine “he whom”: the object is a reality, a message, before it is a person — and yet it is “handled.” Brown (Anchor Bible) takes the neuter as deliberately broad, the whole Christ-event; Marshall (NICNT) reads through it to the person."
  },
