   "body": "ἦν (imperfect) → ἀκηκόαμεν, ἑωράκαμεν (perfect) → ἐθεασάμεθα, ἐψηλάφησαν (aorist). The majority view is that the choice encodes aspect — how the author frames the action — more than time. What “perfect” itself means is contested: Porter (stative), Fanning (blended), Campbell (proximity)."
